# Metamorphic fuzzer: multi-relation SELECTs (joins of every kind, self-joins)
# checked against five relations decided by SQL semantics alone -- TLP, NoREC,
# multi-relation mode agreement, join commutativity (A JOIN B == B JOIN A with
# the kind flipped, the only one that varies the build side), and aggregate
# decomposition (one-shot == group-then-re-aggregate, which drives the
# partial/final merge and AggState spill serde). Finds SEMANTIC bugs (wrong
# answers every execution mode agrees on). Default budget is small (each case
# runs the engine several times), part of `bazel test //...`.
